<p>A ceasefire meant to halt fighting involving Iran, the United States, and Israel came under strain almost immediately, as Gulf Arab countries reported fresh Iranian missile and drone attacks within hours of the truce announcement. Regional and international outlets said Bahrain, Kuwait, Qatar, the United Arab Emirates, and Saudi energy infrastructure were targeted. Kuwait reported fires at oil, power, and desalination facilities, while Saudi Arabia began assessing damage to its East-West crude pipeline. Some Gulf states also said their air defenses limited the immediate damage. Qatar said its military intercepted seven ballistic missiles and multiple drones, while the UAE said it intercepted 17 ballistic missiles and 35 drones. Iranian state-linked reporting cast the strikes as retaliation after explosions hit oil facilities on Lavan and Sirri islands, with Tehran accusing Kuwait and the UAE of involvement. Together, the exchanges showed how fragile the truce remains and how quickly the conflict has spread across the wider Gulf region.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/ZizAnCq2OmTLGaZVaeRhAec0IggUb1mOizOovk1DpSsf-yXPwQuxsS6TlSqGG4DbyPlrVZB1vWh66CR8kki9ihLpEk19ycreq1BACFr093pWZOgzs0IUFw5aWVVA4b010Stt1jWZxUcdLNjRIY2VciPlEOEZKQa7X1RYGSqaT2kJRtLJfXBGbpQfYE0qTY1_qstPXgLcbzuYboy50xN2_L5YhL2n6x12jJ5ea81W-5SrYAev_3IviJm-eLOSknzNJVsM3fdfFVBXcva8OA' alt='A full moon, or &quot;Blood Moon,&quot; above the Abu Dhabi skyline as regional missile and drone attacks affected Gulf states.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Multi-front attacks: CNBC&#x27;s list of reported targets included Israel as well as Bahrain, Kuwait, Qatar, and the UAE, suggesting the ceasefire breakdown was not limited to the Gulf monarchies.</li><li>Critical services at risk: Kuwait said fires broke out at power and desalination plants as well as oil facilities, showing that the strikes threatened water and electricity systems, not just petroleum assets.</li><li>Shipping danger: Semafor reported that Iran also reportedly closed the Strait of Hormuz in response to Israeli attacks on Lebanon, raising the possibility of disruption at a major maritime energy chokepoint.</li><li>Ceasefire scope dispute: Semafor reported that Washington said Lebanon was not covered by the agreement, suggesting the parties were working from different understandings of what the truce actually included.</li></ul><blockquote>Ceasefires are always messy, - JD Vance</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Iranian state media: Tehran-linked outlets portrayed the attacks on Kuwait and the UAE as a response to blasts at Lavan and Sirri, framing Iran as retaliating for strikes on its own oil infrastructure rather than opening a new front. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/iran-attacked-kuwait-uae-after-strikes-on-its-oil-facilities-state-tv/article70839338.ece'>The Hindu</a>, <a href='https://www.yemenonline.info/gulf-news/12251'>Yemen Online</a>)</li><li>US administration: Washington said it was confident the ceasefire would hold even after the renewed attacks, and Vice President JD Vance described the ongoing hostilities as a misunderstanding tied to the difficulty of putting a ceasefire into effect. (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/04/08/2026/iran-truce-already-in-doubt'>Semafor</a>)</li><li>Gulf governments: Official statements focused on control and continuity. Kuwait emphasized firefighting at strategic utility and oil sites, while Qatar and the UAE highlighted interceptions to show that their air defenses remained operational during the barrage. (<a href='https://www.middleeasteye.net/live-blog/live-blog-update/kuwait-reports-damage-oil-facilities-power-stations-after-iranian-drone'>Middle East Eye</a>, <a href='https://www.yahoo.com/news/articles/qatar-reports-rocket-drone-attacks-163721442.html'>Yahoo</a>, <a href='https://www.thenationalnews.com/news/uae/2026/04/08/uae-intercepts-17-ballistic-missiles-and-35-drones-in-wednesdays-figures/'>The National</a>)</li><li>News analysis: World Politics Review, cited by Semafor, argued that the agreement was a ceasefire in name only because conditions on the ground had changed little in the first 24 hours. (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/04/08/2026/iran-truce-already-in-doubt'>Semafor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/04/08/world/iran-war-trump-news/gulf-countries-attacks-iran-ceasefire'>Gulf Arab nations report a barrage of Iranian attacks since the cease-fire.</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/iran-attacked-kuwait-uae-after-strikes-on-its-oil-facilities-state-tv/article70839338.ece'>Iran attacked Kuwait, UAE after strikes on its oil facilities: State TV</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/04/08/2026/iran-truce-already-in-doubt'>Iran truce already in doubt</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-persian-gulf-countries-ceasefire-missile-strikes-iran/'>For Persian Gulf countries, the ceasefire has meant another day of missile strikes</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.yemenonline.info/gulf-news/12251'>Iranian agencies report explosions from the Lavan and Sirri islands of unknown origin. Iran accuses Kuwait and the UAE of the attacks and launches retaliatory attacks against those countries in response. (Ynet)</a> - yemenonline.info</li><li><a href='https://www.middleeasteye.net/live-blog/live-blog-update/kuwait-reports-damage-oil-facilities-power-stations-after-iranian-drone'>Kuwait&#x27;s interior ministry reports fires at several oil facilities, power plants, and desalination plants after an Iranian drone attack.</a> - middleeasteye.net</li><li><a href='https://www.reuters.com/business/energy/saudi-arabias-east-west-oil-pipeline-hit-iranian-attack-damage-being-assessed-2026-04-08/'>Saudi Arabia&#x27;s East–West Crude Oil Pipeline is hit in an Iranian attack.</a> - reuters.com</li><